# Desktop preview: boots to the compositor, the terminal window takes typed
# input, the mouse can drag a window, open the launcher menu, and start an
# application. Coordinates assume the 1280x800 test display.
ps2mouse: streaming
gui: desktop up
cerberus kernel shell
!key help
!wait 1
cerberus> help
!screenshot build/desktop-1.png
# Resize the About window: over its right edge (x=1220) the cursor turns
# into a two-headed arrow, and dragging moves the edge.
!mouseto 1221 300
!wait 0.3
!screenshot build/desktop-resize-1.png
!button left down
!mouse -100 0
!button left up
!wait 0.5
!screenshot build/desktop-resize-2.png
# Drag the About window by its title bar (now x=760..1120, y=90..122).
!mouseto 1000 105
!button left down
!mouse -220 180
!button left up
!wait 0.5
!screenshot build/desktop-2.png
# Open the launcher menu (the logo button at x=13..53, y=752..790).
!mouseto 28 780
!button left down
!button left up
!wait 0.5
!screenshot build/desktop-3.png
# Pick "System Monitor": the list starts at y=488, 38 per item; third item.
!mouseto 100 583
!button left down
!button left up
!wait 1.5
!screenshot build/desktop-4.png
# Alt+Tab is exercised by the keyboard test; here type into the terminal
# again after clicking it, to prove focus follows the click.
!mouseto 120 470
!button left down
!button left up
!key ticks
!wait 0.5
cerberus> ticks
ticks=
# The calendar (0.0.5g): click the clock, add a reminder for today, and a
# notification from the shell. Then close the System Monitor by its close
# button (its frame is 220,152 520x360) while it fades out.
!mouseto 1200 770
!button left down
!button left up
!wait 0.5
!key 14:30 Call home
!wait 0.5
!screenshot build/desktop-5.png
!mouseto 120 470
!button left down
!button left up
!key notify hello from the shell
!wait 0.6
!screenshot build/desktop-6.png
!mouseto 716 168
!button left down
!button left up
!wait 0.1
!mouseto 120 470
!button left down
!button left up
!key ticks
!wait 0.5
ticks=
!key gui
!wait 0.5
frames
